From 682d57dd1a80b4a30407ab2e5a6525a1d51c4d96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "a.tzitanov" <alexypoloz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 13:52:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(search): bias graph-tool selection + valid
 function-calling history
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Rewrite TOOL_DESCRIPTIONS prescriptively and add tool-routing rules
  to the agent system prompt so the LLM picks graph_search /
  find_entity_by_id for entity/relation questions instead of always
  defaulting to vector_search.
- Record the assistant tool_call turn before each TOOL observation
  (SerializedToolCall + tool_calls field + serde) so the reasoning
  history is a valid assistant→tool pairing instead of orphan tool
  messages — lets the model track prior calls and chain graph steps.
- Add a local Ollama (gemma4:e4b) entry to the LiteLLM config for
  offline agent function-calling tests.

Verified end-to-end against litellm → ollama gemma4:e4b: routing
discriminates correctly and multi-turn history is accepted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
